  "title": "Government Drafts Late Payment Fee Rules for Standalone Battery Storage",
  "summary": "The Ministry of Power has proposed amendments to the late electricity payment surcharge rules, which seek to protect standalone battery energy storage service providers against delayed payments by distribution companies (DISCOMS). The Electricity (Late Payment Surcharge and Related Matters) (Amendment) Rules, 2026, will give independent companies operating standalone storage systems the same protection against delayed payments by DISCOMs that power generators, transmission companies and electricity traders currently enjoy.",
